  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Suppose you have an array B&nbsp;(0≤Bi≤109)B \\ (0 \\leq B_i \\leq 10^9)B&nbsp;(0≤Bi​≤109) of length MMM, and a positive integer K&nbsp;(1≤K&lt;M)K \\ (1 \\leq K \\lt M)K&nbsp;(1≤K&lt;M).\n\nYou are allowed to do the following operation on BBB:\n\n\nSelect xxx indices i1,i2,…,ix&nbsp;(1≤ij≤M)i_1, i_2, \\ldots, i_x \\ (1 \\leq i_j \\leq M)i1​,i2​,…,ix​&nbsp;(1≤ij​≤M), such that (ij+1−ij)≥K(i_{j + 1} - i_j) \\geq K(ij+1​−ij​)≥K for all 1≤j&lt;x1 \\leq j \\lt x1≤j&lt;x;\nSubtract 111 to BijB_{i_j}Bij​​ for all 1≤j≤x1 \\leq j \\leq x1≤j≤x.\nFor the array BBB and integer KKK, let `score`(B,K)(B, K)(B,K) denote the **minimum** number of operations required to make all the elements of BBB equal to 000.\n\nYou are given an array AAA consisting of NNN non-negative integers, and a positive integer PPP.\n\nFind the value ∑i=1N∑j=iNF(i,j)\\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\sum_{j=i}^{N} F(i,j)∑i=1N​∑j=iN​F(i,j), where F(i,j)=F(i,j)=F(i,j)= `score`(A[i,j],P)(A[i,j],P)(A[i,j],P).\n\nSince the sum might be too large, please print it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\nNote that A[i,j]A[i, j]A[i,j] denotes the subarray [Ai,Ai+1,…,Aj][A_i, A_{i+1}, \\ldots, A_j][Ai​,Ai+1​,…,Aj​].\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first line of each test case contains two positive integers NNN and PPP −-− the length of AAA and the parameter integer PPP.\nThe second line contains NNN space separated integers, A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ −-− denoting the array AAA.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print on a new line, the required sum modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤P&lt;N≤1061 \\leq P \\lt N \\leq 10^61≤P&lt;N≤106",
      "0≤Ai≤1090 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^90≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
